            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to wrestle, then the Persian for weightlifting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: نرمش کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نرمش کردن (narmesh kardan) — \"to stretch, to do light exercises\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قبل از دویدن نرمش میکنم. qabl az davidan narmesh mikonam. I stretch before running."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "narmesh 'suppleness', from narm 'soft', + kardan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "narmesh is built on native Persian narm, 'soft', with the noun ending -esh: softening the body. EtymDB has no entry for it. kardan is inherited."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
